<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 2 September, from 44 BCE to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/cicero" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cicero.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/44-bce">44 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,069 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cicero delivers the first Philippic against Mark Antony</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a speech to the Senate, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cicero">Cicero</a> criticised the legislation of the consuls <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and Publius Cornelius Dolabella as contrary to the will of the late Caesar. It was the first of 14 speeches against Antony, known as the Philippics.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cicero">Cicero</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/44-bce">44 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,069 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cleopatra VII makes her son Caesarion co-ruler of Egypt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleopatra-vii">Cleopatra VII</a> made her son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caesarion">Caesarion</a>, by her account the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>, co-ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> as Ptolemy XV. He reigned with her until 30 BCE, when Octavian had him put to death, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic dynasty</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caesarion">Caesarion</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleopatra-vii">Cleopatra VII</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/31-bce">31 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,056 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Octavian defeats Antony and Cleopatra at Actium</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Octavian's fleet under Agrippa defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and Cleopatra off Actium in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. Their flight to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> left Octavian, soon to be Augustus, master of the Roman world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1192">1192 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">834 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard I and Saladin agree the Treaty of Jaffa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Shortly after the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffa">Jaffa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, agreed a three-year truce, negotiated with the help of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balian-of-ibelin">Balian of Ibelin</a>. The treaty, signed on 1 or 2 September, ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-jaffa-1192">Treaty of Jaffa</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1666">1666 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">360 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Great Fire of London breaks out in Pudding Lane</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fire broke out in Thomas Farriner's bakery and raged for four days, destroying some 13,200 houses, 87 churches and old St Paul's Cathedral. Wren's rebuilding transformed the City.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1792">1792 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The September Massacres begin in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fearing a Prussian advance and a plot among prisoners, crowds broke into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> prisons and killed some 1,100 to 1,400 inmates over five days. The massacres foreshadowed the Terror.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japan signs the instrument of surrender aboard USS Missouri</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese envoys signed the formal surrender in Tokyo Bay before General MacArthur and Allied representatives. The ceremony officially ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uss-missouri">USS Missouri</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">CBS Evening News becomes America's first half-hour network newscast</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Walter Cronkite's evening news on CBS expanded from 15 to 30 minutes, opening with an interview with President Kennedy. NBC followed within a week, setting the format of US network news.</p></div></li></ol>
